un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 3,1 a 9,3. En diciembre se adjudicó el 20 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 12 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 27 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.250 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos al límite no implica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones como la necesidad de un servicio o a precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si en diciembre se adjudicaron otros contratos al límite. Analizar si los adjudicatarios repiten contratos en distintas fechas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 30 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 5.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.1 to 9.3. December accounts for 20% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. Contract [1], for 14,250 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [3], for 14,890 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper behavior. Small amounts just under the limit can result from market prices or budget constraints. Statistical patterns do not prove wrongdoing in individual cases.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases. Review the November contract to see if it aligns with other contracts. Look for patterns in awardees to determine if multiple contracts served the same purpose.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["7Ov5xv%2FZQXiS81gZFETW